title Replacing old messages with a summary

surface "Model's view"
request "Summary request"
model "DeepSeek"
record "Record events" counter 8

surface -> request -> model -> surface

range at surface

# The view is too large, so messages 1 to 3 must become shorter.
pause "Messages 1 to 3 cost 2,150 tokens. The record already holds 8 events."

# The start marker goes into the record before any other work.
record +1 "compaction/start is seq 8. It does not join the view."

# The old range goes out in one request, after the same system prompt.
range -> request : waiting "The same start bytes as the last step give a cache hit."
range -> model : running "A final user message asks for a structured summary."

# The model writes a summary that is smaller than the range.
new summary at model
range : done "250 tokens replace 2,150, so the summary is accepted."

# The summary is recorded, then takes the place of the range in the view.
summary -> surface 1200ms "seq 10 replaces seqs 1 to 3; the view is now 0, 10, 4, 5, 6, 7."
record +2
remove range

# The end marker comes last, so a crash leaves a start without an end.
record +1 "compaction/end is seq 11. All 12 events remain in the record."
